#: missions/gdl_03/mission.json
msgid "The delegation's cart or the council's envoys are destroyed"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_03/mission.json
msgid "The envoys stop in each of the three villages on the way and go on once a church stands there. Lay the next church before they come."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_08/mission.json
msgid "The evening of the seventh of September. The camp by the Dnieper. At the entrance to the hetman's tent sits a scribe with an inkwell at his belt. Andrei comes up. The scribe reads his name in the list and looks up."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_03/mission.json
msgid "The evidence at the top right is what the Order can show the council. At 100 the mission is lost. Every baptized peasant slows it down."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_01/mission.json
msgid "The field between Grunwald, Stębark and Ludwikowo, Prussia. 15 July 1410."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_02/mission.json
msgid "The field by Grunwald, Prussia. 15 July 1410."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_03/mission.json
msgid "The fire in the alka has gone under the ground: the grove gives half its Power from now on."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_08/mission.json
msgid "The first bridge stands. The foot and the guns can go over it slowly, a few at a time."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "The first on the wall was Jakub of Kobylany, and after him Dobiesław of Oleśnica. Twenty-five years later Jakub will lead the Crown's knights at Wiłkomierz, but that is another story, and I have told it already."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_08/mission.json
msgid "The ford is upstream, to the east: the light horse and the lances can cross it, the guns cannot. Send the camp servants to the two marked places on the bank: standing there they lay a bridge section by section (40 wood each, the wagons bring more). A Muscovite patrol rides the far bank at night: if it watches your men for long, the alarm goes up."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_05/mission.json
msgid "The ford lies below the bridge, towards the Dnieper. No more than two in it at once: whoever crowds in drowns. Leave a rearguard on the near bank. Four light horse whose standard-bearer fell have joined you."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_06/mission.json
msgid "The forest borderland of Muscovy and the Grand Duchy of Lithuania. The end of August or September 1507."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "The garrison has broken into the royal camp and ruined the king's tent."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "The garrison sends riders to catch the envoys. An envoy with an enemy at his side and none of ours near is taken. Every sworn town sends food, powder or silver."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_08/mission.json
msgid "The general attack! The foot and the guns are yours again, and the hetman gives you ten more banners of horse. Chelyadnin will throw his reserves into the field one after another. Muscovite banners that have lost heart and are caught between your men from two sides give themselves up."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_01/mission.json
msgid "The great banner of the kingdom lies in the dust. The Polish banners waver and break."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_01/mission.json
msgid "The great banner of the kingdom lies on the ground longer than 60 seconds"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_08/mission.json
msgid "The grove is there still. My grandfather Mikołaj used to say he had a brother, Jurij, who went away east."
msgstr ""

#: ui/tips.gd
msgid "The heart of your land: trains peasants, takes in every resource and leads your people into the next age. In a skirmish, a side that loses every town centre and castle is out."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_07/mission.json
msgid "The hetman and his army are on the road to Orsha. Glinski has no time for Slutsk now."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_06/mission.json
msgid "The hetman himself said afterwards that a local woman who knew the paths led him through the bog. But Andrei swore that he saw wolves that night, going along the bank in a pack, and all of them one way."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_05/mission.json
msgid "The hetman leaves last, standard-bearer. Lead your men away. That is an order."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_08/mission.json
msgid "The hetman's headquarters falls or the army is thrown into the Dnieper"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_08/mission.json
msgid "The hetman's headquarters has fallen. The army breaks and runs for the river."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_05/mission.json
msgid "The hetman's ring holds: %s"
msgstr ""

#: ui/help_panel.gd
msgid "The hints at the top left can be turned off in the settings."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_06/mission.json
msgid "The horses are ready, prince."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_05/mission.json
msgid "The horses in the forest are moving! The ambush will strike in half a minute."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_02/mission.json
msgid "The khan is taking his men away. Don't stand there, Lithuanian, or you will stay here for good."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_01/mission.json
msgid "The king has fallen. The army has lost its head."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_01/mission.json
msgid "The king is killed or taken"
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "The king orders."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "The king orders: do not go into the breach! Fall back to the church!"
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "The king rides past with his suite. He looks at the castle for a long time and says nothing."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_08/mission.json
msgid "The king wrote afterwards to the sovereigns and to Rome that the Muscovites were eighty thousand and that thirty thousand of them fell or were taken. I wrote the lists of captives in my own hand, and I know that kings count otherwise than scribes do. The master of the horse Chelyadnin we took captive, and Smolensk we never won back."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_01/mission.json
msgid "The king's hill. A lone knight of the Order with his lance lowered rides straight at Jagiełło. A young scribe without armour catches up a broken lance and strikes the knight in the side; he falls. The king strikes him with his own lance, the guard finishes him."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "The king's tent is ruined"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_01/mission.json
msgid "The knights are coming out! Don't let them reach the boats!"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_02/mission.json
msgid "The lance beside Gintaut carries his banner. Units near it keep their spirit. If the bearer falls, bring a rider to the banner within 20 seconds, or the khorugv runs."
msgstr ""

#: ui/hud.gd
msgid "The last capital cannot be taken apart"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_03/mission.json
msgid "The last village, my lord. From here the road goes to Medininkai."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_02/mission.json
msgid "The lone oak on the hill is a place of power. Take it, and the znakharka can lay an alka there for Power."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_01/mission.json
msgid "The lord vogt demands grain for the castles. You wanted to be protected, did you not?"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_04/mission.json
msgid "The marshal's banner is down! Press on, lords, before they raise another!"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_03/mission.json
msgid "The mist lies over the grove. The envoys pass by without seeing the oak."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "The north side is open now. The sorties will come out of the north gate too."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "The northern camp. The Lithuanians are striking their tents. The Tatars drive their herds from the meadows. Vytautas rides up to the king's tent, pale."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_03/mission.json
msgid "The oak has fallen and the alka with it: the evidence fell by 20. The pagans at the farmstead grow in number."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_05/mission.json
msgid "The old branch of our family stayed in Samogitia and Vilnius. The younger went to the Dnieper, became Orthodox and served the princes. Andrei Gintovt was of the younger branch. That year he was twenty, and he carried the banner for the first time."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_01/mission.json
msgid "The old men argued afterwards who led ours then: the sword-bearer Zyndram or the marshal. Jaśko remembered Zyndram, because he shouted louder than anyone."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_08/mission.json
msgid "The old oak above the Kropivna has given one charge of Power: the znakharka can lay «Bog Mist» once. Under the mist the guns stay hidden even outside the ravine."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_06/mission.json
msgid "The old woman does not answer and goes ahead without looking back. The prince gets down and leads his horse by the bridle. The barking behind them falters and goes off to one side, as if the patrol had turned the wrong way. In the middle of the causeway the old woman is gone; only the lantern hangs on a pole."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_06/mission.json
msgid "The other bank. Dawn twilight. Andrei with a patrol by the water."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_03/mission.json
msgid "The pagans are coming out of the farmstead again."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_03/mission.json
msgid "The pagans are going for the new church."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_03/mission.json
msgid "The pagans from the farmstead are coming for the church. You can buy peace at the farmstead: bring Gintaut there."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_03/mission.json
msgid "The pagans lie in wait on the hills!"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_03/mission.json
msgid "The pagans will leave you alone for the rest of this chapter."
msgstr ""

#: ui/mission_panel.gd
msgid "The patrol has raised the alarm"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_08/mission.json
msgid "The patrol has seen us! They are riding off to Orsha!"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_01/mission.json
msgid "The pier is ours. No more boats will come to Skirsnemune."
msgstr ""

#: ui/ui_text.gd
msgid "The place is taken"
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "The plague grows with the crowding, the heat and with men standing on the canal below the town. A priest and an infirmary bring it down, but never to nothing. When it is high your healers do not heal and the men waste away."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "The plague in the camp reaches its limit"
msgstr ""

#: ui/tips.gd
msgid "The price is for each cell of the line."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_01/mission.json
msgid "The priest can set up a wayside cross on a place of power. Each cross gives Power for «Bogurodzica»."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_06/mission.json
msgid "The prince is gone! Bring the dogs! And tell the voivode: if we do not find him, they will ask it of us as of traitors."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_05/mission.json
msgid "The prince says: he has seen. And that we are to hold the right edge."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_01/mission.json
msgid "The prince's. Prince Vytautas has not sent us yet. But the Germans held back the king's grain, and now the prince says he did not send us far enough."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_02/mission.json
msgid "The pursuers have lost their order. Turn on them now: a turn right after a retreat strikes hard."
msgstr ""

#: ui/ui_text.gd
msgid "The queue is full"
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "The ransom for the guest knight you took at Grunwald has been paid: 100 silver."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_07/mission.json
msgid "The rebels break camp in %s"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_07/mission.json
msgid "The rebels come in %s"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_07/mission.json
msgid "The rebels have gone. Slutsk has held."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_07/mission.json
msgid "The rebels have taken the Upper castle."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_03/mission.json
msgid "The road through the grove is boggy. Let us go over the hills, my lord."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "The road to Sztum. A column of wagons with bombards in the dust. Jaśko rides at the tail and looks back at the castle."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "The round tower. A piece of masonry crashes down from above. When the dust settles a knight sits on the ground, alive, but his helmet is crushed flat. They lead him to the field forge. The smith takes aim with his hammer."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "The royal council did refuse to bribe the Czechs, calling it unknightly. Who first put the thought forward was not written down. Pan Jan said his great-grandfather did, and that the one in red had prompted him. Forty-seven years later the Crown will buy Malbork from Czech hirelings after all, and it will cost a hundred and ninety thousand florins."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_01/mission.json
msgid "The second Mass. If the Germans roast in their pots before noon, there will be nobody left for us to fight."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_04/mission.json
msgid "The second night. At dawn Švitrigaila's army will move."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_07/mission.json
msgid "The secret passage starts by the court in the Upper castle and comes out on the river bank to the north. Every workshop burned puts the next assault off by a minute. Order your men to set a workshop on fire, then come back."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_01/mission.json
msgid "The shaft is pinned down by a dead horse. Jaśko jumps from the saddle and pulls; it will not come. Beside him a hand in a red sleeve takes hold of the shaft. A man without armour, in a red kaftan, with merry eyes. The fight seems to flow around him."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "The siege is lifted, and the guns have come to Sztum."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_05/mission.json
msgid "The sun goes down to the west, the shadows grow long. Moscow brings fresh men into the field again and again."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "The town is ours. A battery by St John's church stands under cover of its stone: the castle's balls do it less harm."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_03/mission.json
msgid "The truth. That we were baptized. That for years the Germans burned our yards and took our people. That we want the cross, but not the German cross."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_01/mission.json
msgid "The village burns down"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_01/mission.json
msgid "The village has burned down."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_01/mission.json
msgid "The village ran out of food and starved."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_02/mission.json
msgid "The wagon fort! Strike the wagon fort before they come to their senses!"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_04/mission.json
msgid "The wagons bring food, wood, iron and silver to the field camp every minute. Camp servants can put up a stable, an archery range and an alka; hire light horse and archers there."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_06/mission.json
msgid "The watch sees in a cone the way it faces: half as far at night, further with a torch, twice as far into a campfire's light. Their dogs smell whoever comes near, and a trot is heard even behind their backs. Keep to the forest: the prince is not seen there at all, his servants only close up."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_01/mission.json
msgid "The znakharka can call Bog Mist: your units in it cannot be seen until they attack."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "The «Siege» bar is not the damage to the walls but the hunger in the castle. The garrison mends the walls every night; only time and the shot starve them."
msgstr ""

#: ui/command_panel.gd
msgid "Then click your building."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_07/mission.json
msgid "Then men who know how to retreat. You will not need that skill here. We have nowhere to retreat to."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_07/mission.json
msgid "Then the castle must stand until tomorrow, mother."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_04/mission.json
msgid "Then the prince and I take the head, and you the middle. And mind, lord, in the middle ride the Ruthenian banners. Won't your hand shake?"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_02/mission.json
msgid "Then two heralds came from the Master and brought two swords. On one shield was the black eagle of the King of the Romans, on the other the griffin of Szczecin. They said: here are swords for you, if your own are too few, and choose the field, if you are afraid."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_01/mission.json
msgid "There are fish in the lake and honey in the hives. The Germans cannot search the whole forest."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_05/mission.json
msgid "There is a ford lower down, I watered my horse there! Two at a time, not in a crowd! Whoever goes in all at once will drown."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "There is the sign! All their elders are sitting there now, under one pillar!"
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "These are no knechts! Who are they?"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_07/mission.json
msgid "They are leaving. They did not even take the ladders."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_05/mission.json
msgid "They are not running. They are leaving. See how evenly? Hold the line!"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_04/mission.json
msgid "They are tying up the wagons and putting out the fires early. They are leaving for Vilkomir."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_08/mission.json
msgid "They are watching their own bridges, at Orsha. And we are building ours."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_01/mission.json
msgid "They brought these for us. They knew how it would end."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_01/mission.json
msgid "They cut down the old oak."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_01/mission.json
msgid "They did not know. They thought they knew."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_05/mission.json
msgid "They have an icon, and we have an icon. Whom will God help, then?"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_01/mission.json
msgid "They have been coughing for a whole week. Did you do this to them?"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_02/mission.json
msgid "They have long been waiting for it, prince."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_04/mission.json
msgid "They know three. The middle one leads straight to their wagons."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_04/mission.json
msgid "They met at a lake near Vilkomir and stood. And my grandfather Mikołaj stood on the east shore and counted the fires on the west. He hoped his brother was not sitting at one of them."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_05/mission.json
msgid "They run! Moscow runs!"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_02/mission.json
msgid "They say a thunderstorm passed over the field in that hour, and lightning struck where the Germans stood. They say. I would like to believe it."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_08/mission.json
msgid "They say old Gintaut laughed when he was asked whether the Lithuanians ran at Grunwald. Now I understand why. Sound the retreat!"
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "They say that in the Summer Refectory the Germans held council under one pillar, and a traitor hung a red cap in the window, and ours fired at the pillar and missed. The ball in the wall above the fireplace is shown to this day. But everyone tells it his own way, and that only happens with tales. And Jaśko, pan Jan said, stood a long time after that shot looking at what red thing had been in that window."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_01/mission.json
msgid "They say the mist rose from the bog in broad daylight, and a German patrol passed ten steps from our men and saw no one. Such mists do happen in Samogitia. But grandfather said that one was special."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_08/mission.json
msgid "They sing the same as we do, lord standard-bearer."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_08/mission.json
msgid "They sing the same. But they came for something else."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_04/mission.json
msgid "They took forty-two princes captive. They took Prince Sigismund Korybutovich too, who had fought alongside the Czech heretics, and he soon died. Of what he died they write differently, and I will not choose."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_01/mission.json
msgid "They took the bread, now the grove. Take up your spears."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_03/mission.json
msgid "They will not ask about the grove. And if they ask, say that we have plenty of firewood."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_04/mission.json
msgid "They will take the land anyway."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_08/mission.json
msgid "This I saw myself. Thunder without lightning, as a Samogitian once said at Grunwald. Only now the powder was dry, and the guns were ours."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_06/mission.json
msgid "This time you found it yourself, prince."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_02/mission.json
msgid "This too Długosz wrote down. They knocked the helmet off with hammers, and pan Piotr lived."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_03/mission.json
msgid "Three years after the great battle King Jogaila and Grand Duke Vytautas came to Samogitia to baptize it, and Gintaut was among the first to step into the river. Now the Order says that the Samogitians are baptized in name only, and its spies are gathering evidence for the council at Konstanz."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_03/mission.json
msgid "Three years after the great battle, King Jogaila and Grand Duke Vytautas came to Samogitia themselves. Długosz writes that they cut down the groves and put out the fires. Great-grandfather did not tell it so. He said that it was cold, and that the king spoke to the people in our tongue."
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_01/mission.json
msgid "Throw back the blow of the Order's right wing"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_02/mission.json
msgid "Thunder without lightning!"
msgstr ""

#: game/arena/arena.gd
msgid "Time: %d s"
msgstr ""

#: ui/mission_panel.gd
msgid "Tired"
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_01/mission.json
msgid "To horse! We go at the signal, not before. Whoever jumps out first for glory, the Germans will take first."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_05/mission.json
msgid "To the bridge! Everyone to the bridge!"
msgstr ""

#: missions/crown_01/mission.json
msgid "To the wagons! Strike their wagenburg before they come to their senses!"
msgstr ""

#: ui/advisor.gd
msgid "To win, destroy the enemy's capital, or hold every place of power for 5 minutes."
msgstr ""

#: ui/tips.gd
msgid "Towers, walls and gates see 2 cells farther."
msgstr ""

#: ui/mission_panel.gd
msgid "Towns sworn: %d"
msgstr ""

#: ui/tips.gd
msgid "Trains archers and crossbowmen."
msgstr ""

#: ui/tips.gd
msgid "Trains foot soldiers."
msgstr ""

#: ui/tips.gd
msgid "Trains horsemen."
msgstr ""

#: ui/tips.gd
msgid "Trains: %s"
msgstr ""

#: ui/command_panel.gd
msgid "Turn and face the chasers at once."
msgstr ""

#: ui/command_panel.gd
msgid "Turn around"
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_08/mission.json
msgid "Two armies face each other. Over both of them icons. On both sides they sing the same words."
msgstr ""

#: missions/gdl_02/mission.json
msgid "Two fresh Lithuanian banners have gathered at the forest. The reserve is going for the Poles: strike it in the flank before it breaks through. The znakharka can call Perkūnas's Wrath on it."
msgstr ""

#: ui/unit_card.gd
msgid "Under construction: %d%%"
msgstr ""

#: ui/end_screen.gd
msgid "Units killed"
msgstr ""

#: ui/end_screen.gd
msgid "Units lost"
msgstr ""

#: ui/end_screen.gd
msgid "Units trained"
msgstr ""

#: ui/tips.gd
msgid "Units walk over it"
msgstr ""

#: ui/tips.gd
msgid "Unseen in the forest until it shoots"
msgstr ""

